  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Why does this matter?"
   ],
   [
    1.393,
    "Think of a lake in winter."
   ],
   [
    2.956,
    "As water cools, it gets denser, until about four degrees Celsius, where it is at its densest."
   ],
   [
    9.427,
    "Colder water, just above freezing, begins to lock into the lattice, so it expands and stays near the top."
   ],
   [
    16.784,
    "At the surface it freezes, and the ice floats as a lid."
   ],
   [
    20.378,
    "That lid slows the heat leaving the water below, so the lake stays liquid underneath, and the fish survive."
   ],
   [
    26.992,
    "If ice sank, lakes would freeze from the bottom up, and could freeze solid."
   ]
  ]
